    "short": "Thirumarperu Manikandeswarar Temple is a Hindu temple dedicated to Shiva on Ocheri-Tirumalpur road in Tirumalpur, Tamil Nadu, India.",
    "description": "Thirumarperu Manikandeswarar Temple is a Hindu temple dedicated to Shiva on Ocheri-Tirumalpur road in Tirumalpur, Tamil Nadu, India. Constructed in the Dravidian style of architecture, the temple is believed to have been built during the Cholas period in the 9th century. Shiva is worshipped as Manikandeswarar and his consort Parvathi as Karunai Nayagi. The presiding deity is revered in the 7th century Tamil Saiva canonical work, the Tevaram, written by Tamil saint poets known as the Nayanmars and classified as Paadal Petra Sthalam.",
